text(await tools.mcp__codex_app__create_thread({
title:"Bring Baste’s persona companion into Studio",
target:{type:"project",projectId:"4259fd71-bfc4-4958-9492-47a6c8905cdb",environment:{type:"worktree",startingState:{type:"working-tree"}}},
prompt:`Implement the user's Baste companion-designer experience, carrying forward the existing working tree. The user has authorized construction of the missing connection and sign-in readiness, and wants a beautiful, lively Studio centered on a persona representing the target audience, with whom the designer can communicate and co-design the application. The persona's cultural world should drive colors, tokens, fonts, spacing, edges, motion, iconography, imagery, textures, assets, and component choices.

Current user feedback: existing forms are ugly, disconnected, and dump too much on users at once. They admire Twyne's brief/interview components and want richer, step-based briefing and persona forms with fluid conversational patterns. Studio aesthetic-profile controls already show useful axes such as motion, edges, temperature, density, layout, and hand-drawn/handcrafted/smooth iconography; preserve and deepen this foundation. The tokens panel is useful, although the Cyberbotanist motion feels awkward. Built-in/default personas have empty moodboards, sparse taste and asset examples, and only brief descriptions. The persona must be prominent: an example character image/portrait, a richer cultural/personality description, and a working way to communicate. The experience should feel alive and serve actual design work. Finish the account/sign-in connection needed to persist and resume it.

